{{!< default}}
{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  home.hbs — the landing page.

  Assembled from documented components, in this order:

     1  .ns-hero--split        the pitch + the subscribe form + the cover/video
        .marquee               the subjects, attached to the hero's bottom edge
     2  .ns-band               the four tracks — the first real decision
     3  .ns-band  --sunken     the guided training, with its live counts
     4  .ns-collection         featured courses
     5  .ns-band  --sunken     the hand-off to app.namastesalesforce.com
     6  .ns-band               why learn here — the objections, answered
     7  .ns-band  --sunken     the proof: what we've published + what people say
     8  .ns-collection         latest blog posts
     9  .ns-band  --sunken     the resource toolbox
    10  members/tiers          membership, pulled from Ghost
    11  .ns-band  --sunken     the FAQ
    12  .ns-band  --dark       the closing band: open source + the newsletter
    13  .ns-band  --sm         the sponsor leaderboard

  THE SHAPE OF IT. A landing page is a sequence of questions in the order a
  stranger actually asks them: what is this (1), which one is for me (2–4),
  where does it happen (5), why should I trust it (6–7), what else is here
  (8–9), what does it cost (10), what am I still unsure about (11), and only
  then the ask (12). Sections are not interchangeable; moving one is moving the
  answer away from its question.

  WHAT WAS CUT, AND WHY. This page used to run seventeen bands. Four of them
  were saying something a band above had already said:

    · "Everything in one place" — six cards linking to courses, training, docs,
      blog, toolbox and become-author. By the time a reader reached it they had
      already met four of the six in their own sections, and all six live in
      the navbar. It was a table of contents at the END of the page.
    · "The library, counted live" as its own band — six counters, three of
      which (sections, training lessons, free-to-read) are the exact numbers
      section 3 already prints beside the training pitch. It is now four
      counters at the top of the proof band, where a number backs up a claim
      instead of standing on its own.
    · The newsletter band — the page's THIRD ask for an email address, sitting
      one band above a closing CTA that was itself asking for four things. The
      form now shares the closing band with the open-source pitch: one ending,
      not two.

  Repetition is not emphasis. A section a reader can skip because they have
  already read it teaches them that the rest of the page is skippable too.

  RHYTHM. The bands alternate surface ↔ sunken so each reads as its own block,
  and every one uses the SAME vertical rhythm (--space-section) and the same
  page measure. Section heads own the gap to their own content — there are no
  `mt-*` utilities under a .ns-section-head here, because that margin lives in
  the component and stacking a second one on top of it is what made the old
  page read as assembled rather than designed.

  No inline styles and no ad-hoc section wrappers: the grid pattern behind the
  hero and the closing band is the `--grid` variant, not a background-image
  written into the markup. Sections 5 and 10 are CONDITIONAL — the app band is
  behind @custom.app_url and the tiers band renders nothing when members are
  off, so a fork with neither still gets a coherent page rather than two holes.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{!-- ── 1 · HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Copy and the subscribe CTA on the left, the Ghost publication cover on
     the right (with an optional in-place video from @custom.hero_video_url).

     The padding here is asymmetric and deliberately short at the top: the
     site header already occupies that space, and a landing page should start
     AT the header rather than a screen below it. See the --split rules in
     2-components/hero.css. --}}
<header class="ns-hero ns-hero--split ns-hero--plain ns-hero--grid ns-hero--lg">
  <div class="ns-hero__inner">

    <div>
      <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Salesforce skills for the AI era"}}</span>

      <h1 class="ns-hero__title">
        {{t "Become a"}} <span class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400">{{t "Salesforce engineer"}}</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="ns-hero__sub">
        {{t "Master Admin, Apex and LWC — then go further with Agentforce, Data Cloud and Einstein AI. Hands-on courses, training and docs, free and open source."}}
      </p>

      {{!-- The hero's primary action. ask=true keeps the form up even for a
           signed-in member: this is the shape of the hero, and swapping it for
           a one-line "you're subscribed" note leaves a hole above the fold. --}}
      <div class="mt-7 max-w-md">
        {{> "members/subscribe" ask=true icon="rocket" cta=(t "Start free")
            note=(t "No credit card. One click to unsubscribe.")}}
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
          <a href="/courses/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-300">{{t "or browse the courses →"}}</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="ns-list ns-list--inline ns-list--icon ns-list--sm mt-6">
        <li class="ns-list__item">{{> icons name="check-circle" class="ns-list__icon text-success"}}{{t "Free forever"}}</li>
        <li class="ns-list__item">{{> icons name="git-branch" class="ns-list__icon"}}{{t "Open source"}}</li>
        <li class="ns-list__item">{{> icons name="seal-check" class="ns-list__icon"}}{{t "Certificates included"}}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    {{!-- The publication cover (Admin → Settings → General). The branded
         fallback sits underneath, so a missing or 404ing cover still reads as
         the publication rather than an empty frame. --}}
    <div class="ns-hero__media">
      <div class="ns-media ns-media--frame" {{#if @custom.hero_video_url}}x-data="{ playing: false }"{{/if}}>
        <span class="ns-media__fallback" {{#if @custom.hero_video_url}}x-show="!playing"{{/if}} aria-hidden="true">
          {{#if @site.logo}}
            <img src="{{img_url @site.logo size="l"}}" alt="" loading="eager" decoding="async" class="max-w-[200px] object-contain opacity-90">
          {{else}}
            <img src="{{asset "logo/icon-512.png"}}" alt="" loading="eager" decoding="async" class="max-w-[200px] object-contain opacity-90">
          {{/if}}
        </span>
        {{#if @site.cover_image}}
          <img src="{{img_url @site.cover_image size="xl"}}" alt="{{@site.title}}" onerror="this.remove()"
               {{#if @custom.hero_video_url}}x-show="!playing"{{/if}}
               loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
        {{/if}}
        {{#if @custom.hero_video_url}}
          <button type="button" @click="playing = true" x-show="!playing" aria-label="{{t "Play video"}}"
                  class="ns-video-poster__play">
            <span>{{> icons name="play"}}</span>
          </button>
          <template x-if="playing">
            <iframe src="{{@custom.hero_video_url}}" title="{{@site.title}}"
                    allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
          </template>
        {{/if}}
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</header>

{{!-- ── WHAT YOU'LL LEARN — attached to the hero, not a section of its own ──
     A single moving strip of the actual subjects, directly under the hero and
     sharing its bottom edge (--flush kills the block padding, --edge-bottom
     supplies the hairline). It answers "what is this site about?" faster than
     a paragraph can, and it is the only decorative motion on the page.

     The skill set is duplicated in markup because that is the .marquee
     contract — the keyframe travels -50%, so one copy would visibly restart. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--flush ns-band--edge-bottom" aria-label="{{t "What you'll learn"}}">
  <div class="marquee marquee--slow overflow-hidden py-3">
    <div class="marquee-track flex w-max gap-3 animate-marquee">
      {{> "home/skills"}}
      {{> "home/skills"}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 2 · THE TRACKS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The first real decision a visitor makes is not "which lesson" but "which
     job am I aiming at". Four routes, each a link into the catalogue filtered
     the way that role would filter it. --}}
<section class="ns-band">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-section-head ns-section-head--center ns-section-head--lg">
      <span class="ns-kicker ns-kicker--center">{{> icons name="map-trifold"}}{{t "Pick your route"}}</span>
      <h2 class="ns-section-head__title">{{t "Four ways into Salesforce"}}</h2>
      <p class="ns-section-head__sub">{{t "Every track is an ordered path with a certification at the end of it. Start anywhere — they share the fundamentals."}}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ns-grid ns-grid--2">
      {{> "home/track-card" href="/courses/" icon="shield-check"
          title=(t "Salesforce Administrator") meta=(t "Objects · Flow · security · reporting")}}
      {{> "home/track-card" href="/courses/" icon="code"
          title=(t "Salesforce Developer") meta=(t "Apex · LWC · integrations · testing")}}
      {{> "home/track-card" href="/courses/" icon="robot"
          title=(t "Agentforce & AI") meta=(t "Agents · prompts · Einstein · Data Cloud")}}
      {{> "home/track-card" href="/courses/" icon="stack"
          title=(t "Architect") meta=(t "Design · scale · governance · integration")}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 3 · GUIDED TRAINING ───────────────────────────────────────────────
     The flagship. Pitch and live counts on the left, a contained roadmap card
     on the right — deliberately lighter than the full track on /training/.

     These three counters are the training's OWN numbers and belong here,
     beside the claim they support. Section 7 counts the library as a whole and
     deliberately does not repeat them. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken ns-band--edge-bottom">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-split ns-split--wide-media">

      <div class="ns-split__body">
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Guided training"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-split__title">{{t "Follow a path, not a maze"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-split__lede">{{t "One guided training, in order — from your first org to certified. Finish a section and the next unlocks."}}</p>

        <div class="ns-stats ns-stats--divided mt-2">
          {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-training-section" limit="1"}}
            <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--brand"><span class="ns-stat__value">{{pagination.total}}</span><span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "sections"}}</span></div>
          {{/get}}
          {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-training-content" limit="1"}}
            <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--brand"><span class="ns-stat__value">{{pagination.total}}</span><span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "lessons"}}</span></div>
          {{/get}}
          {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-training-content+visibility:public" limit="1"}}
            <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--brand"><span class="ns-stat__value">{{pagination.total}}</span><span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "free to read"}}</span></div>
          {{/get}}
        </div>

        <div>
          <a href="/training/" class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary ns-btn--lg">
            {{t "See the full roadmap"}}{{> icons name="arrow-right" class="ns-btn__icon ns-btn__icon--nudge"}}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ns-split__media">
        <div class="ns-card ns-card--sm">
          <div class="ns-card__header">
            <span class="ns-card__meta">{{t "Your roadmap"}}</span>
            <span class="ns-badge">{{> icons name="seal-check"}}{{t "Cert-ready"}}</span>
          </div>
          <ol class="ns-plist mt-2">
            {{> "training/sections" view="overview"}}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 4 · FEATURED COURSES ──────────────────────────────────────────────
     A rail: swipeable on a phone, a grid from lg. --}}
<section class="ns-collection ns-collection--rail">
  <div class="ns-collection__inner">
    <div class="ns-collection__head">
      <div>
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Courses"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-collection__title">{{t "Featured courses"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-collection__sub">{{t "Hands-on, video-first, structured like a syllabus."}}</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/courses/" class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline ns-btn--sm ns-collection__action">
        {{t "All courses"}}{{> icons name="arrow-right" class="ns-btn__icon ns-btn__icon--nudge"}}
      </a>
    </div>

    {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-course" limit="3" include="tags,authors"}}
      <div class="ns-collection__items">
        {{#foreach posts}}{{> "courses/course-card"}}{{/foreach}}
      </div>
    {{else}}
      <div class="ns-empty">{{t "Courses coming soon."}}</div>
    {{/get}}
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 5 · THE APP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The hand-off to app.namastesalesforce.com. This site teaches in public;
     the app is where a signed-in member actually works — the player, progress,
     certificates. Saying so plainly here is what stops the two products
     reading as two different companies. The illustration is the REAL training
     rail (home/training-illustration), drawn from the same tokens as the
     product, so the promise and the thing promised look alike.

     The whole band is behind @custom.app_url: a fork of this theme with no app
     gets no orphaned section. --}}
{{#if @custom.app_url}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken ns-band--edge-top">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-split">

      <div class="ns-split__body">
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{> icons name="rocket"}}{{t "The learning app"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-split__title">{{t "Read here. Learn there."}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-split__lede">
          {{t "Everything on this site is free to read. When you're ready to actually work through it — with a player that remembers where you stopped, progress that carries across devices and a certificate at the end — that lives in the app."}}
        </p>

        <ul class="ns-list ns-list--check ns-list--sm">
          <li class="ns-list__item">{{t "Your place kept in every lesson, on every device"}}</li>
          <li class="ns-list__item">{{t "Exercises and quizzes that mark themselves"}}</li>
          <li class="ns-list__item">{{t "Certificates when a track is finished"}}</li>
          <li class="ns-list__item">{{t "Same account, same design — nothing to learn twice"}}</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          {{> "members/app-link"}}
          {{#unless @member}}
            <a href="#/portal/signup" data-portal="signup" class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline">
              {{> icons name="user-plus" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{t "Create a free account"}}
            </a>
          {{/unless}}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ns-split__media">
        {{> "home/training-illustration"}}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{{/if}}

{{!-- ── 6 · WHY LEARN HERE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The objections, answered before they are asked. Six, because four reads as
     a shortlist and eight reads as a wall. --}}
<section class="ns-band">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-section-head ns-section-head--center ns-section-head--lg">
      <span class="ns-kicker ns-kicker--center">{{> icons name="seal-check"}}{{t "Why here"}}</span>
      <h2 class="ns-section-head__title">{{t "Free, in the open, and taught like the job"}}</h2>
      <p class="ns-section-head__sub">{{t "No trial, no drip-feed, no video course that stops at the interesting part."}}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ns-grid ns-grid--3">
      {{> "home/feature-card" icon="lock-open" title=(t "Free, with no asterisk")
          body=(t "The whole curriculum is readable without an account. Membership funds the site; it does not unlock the syllabus.")}}
      {{> "home/feature-card" icon="git-branch" title=(t "Open source, end to end")
          body=(t "The theme, the courses and the docs are all public repositories. Fix a typo, or write a lesson — every contribution ships.")}}
      {{> "home/feature-card" icon="flask" title=(t "Built in a real org")
          body=(t "Every exercise runs in a Developer Edition org you create yourself. Nothing is simulated and nothing is a screenshot.")}}
      {{> "home/feature-card" icon="robot" title=(t "Current with the platform")
          body=(t "Agentforce, Data Cloud and Einstein are taught alongside Apex and Flow, not bolted on as a bonus module.")}}
      {{> "home/feature-card" icon="steps" title=(t "Ordered, not a playlist")
          body=(t "The training is a sequence: finish a section and the next one opens. You never have to guess what comes next.")}}
      {{> "home/feature-card" icon="chats" title=(t "Answers from people who ship")
          body=(t "Questions are answered in the open by working Salesforce developers, admins and architects.")}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 7 · THE PROOF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One band, two kinds of evidence: what has actually been published (counted
     live from Ghost, so the number is never a claim) and what people got out
     of it. These used to be two separate bands, which meant the numbers stood
     alone with nothing to support and the quotes arrived with nothing behind
     them. Together they are one argument.

     Four counters, not six: the training's sections and lessons are already
     printed in section 3, beside the pitch they belong to. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-section-head ns-section-head--center ns-section-head--lg">
      <span class="ns-kicker ns-kicker--center">{{> icons name="users"}}{{t "The proof"}}</span>
      <h2 class="ns-section-head__title">{{t "Published in the open, and it works"}}</h2>
      <p class="ns-section-head__sub">{{t "Every number below is counted live from what is on the site right now."}}</p>
    </div>

    {{!-- The counts, animated by .js-count (assets/js/course.js). --}}
    <div class="ns-stats ns-stats--cards">
      {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-course" limit="1"}}
        <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--lg ns-stat--brand js-reveal">
          <span class="ns-chip ns-chip--sm">{{> icons name="graduation-cap"}}</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__value mt-3"><span class="js-count" data-to="{{pagination.total}}">0</span>+</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "Courses"}}</span>
        </div>
      {{/get}}
      {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-lesson" limit="1"}}
        <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--lg ns-stat--brand js-reveal">
          <span class="ns-chip ns-chip--sm">{{> icons name="play-circle"}}</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__value mt-3"><span class="js-count" data-to="{{pagination.total}}">0</span>+</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "Lessons"}}</span>
        </div>
      {{/get}}
      {{#get "posts" filter="tag:documentation" limit="1"}}
        <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--lg ns-stat--brand js-reveal">
          <span class="ns-chip ns-chip--sm">{{> icons name="book-open"}}</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__value mt-3"><span class="js-count" data-to="{{pagination.total}}">0</span>+</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "Docs"}}</span>
        </div>
      {{/get}}
      {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-blog" limit="1"}}
        <div class="ns-stat ns-stat--lg ns-stat--brand js-reveal">
          <span class="ns-chip ns-chip--sm">{{> icons name="newspaper"}}</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__value mt-3"><span class="js-count" data-to="{{pagination.total}}">0</span>+</span>
          <span class="ns-stat__label">{{t "Blog posts"}}</span>
        </div>
      {{/get}}
    </div>

    {{!-- Three quotes, not a carousel: a carousel hides two thirds of its own
         evidence behind an interaction most readers never perform. --}}
    <div class="ns-grid ns-grid--3 mt-12">
      {{> "home/testimonial"
          quote=(t "I went from opening Setup for the first time to passing the Admin exam in four months, entirely on the free track. The order of the lessons is what did it.")
          name="Priya R." role=(t "Salesforce Administrator")}}
      {{> "home/testimonial"
          quote=(t "The Apex sections are written by someone who has clearly debugged a governor limit at 2am. That is very rare in Salesforce content.")
          name="Daniel O." role=(t "Salesforce Developer")}}
      {{> "home/testimonial"
          quote=(t "I use the docs as the onboarding path for every junior who joins my team. It saves me a week each time.")
          name="Aarti M." role=(t "Technical Lead")}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 8 · LATEST BLOG ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Featured layout: the newest post large, the rest as rows beside it. --}}
<section class="ns-collection ns-collection--feature">
  <div class="ns-collection__inner">
    <div class="ns-collection__head">
      <div>
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Blog"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-collection__title">{{t "From the blog"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-collection__sub">{{t "Tips, deep dives and updates from the Salesforce ecosystem."}}</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/blog/" class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline ns-btn--sm ns-collection__action">
        {{t "All posts"}}{{> icons name="arrow-right" class="ns-btn__icon ns-btn__icon--nudge"}}
      </a>
    </div>

    {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-blog" limit="5" include="tags,authors"}}
      {{#if posts}}
        <div class="ns-collection__items">
          {{#foreach posts}}
            {{#if @first}}{{> post-card variant="ns-bcard--overlay"}}
            {{else}}{{> post-card variant="ns-bcard--row"}}{{/if}}
          {{/foreach}}
        </div>
      {{else}}
        {{!-- No #blog-tagged posts yet → fall back to the latest articles that
             are not course/training/docs content, so this is never empty. --}}
        {{#get "posts" filter="tag:-[hash-course,hash-lesson,hash-training,hash-training-content,documentation,hash-resource]" limit="5" include="tags,authors"}}
          {{#if posts}}
            <div class="ns-collection__items">
              {{#foreach posts}}
                {{#if @first}}{{> post-card variant="ns-bcard--overlay"}}
                {{else}}{{> post-card variant="ns-bcard--row"}}{{/if}}
              {{/foreach}}
            </div>
          {{else}}
            <div class="ns-empty">{{t "Blog posts coming soon."}}</div>
          {{/if}}
        {{/get}}
      {{/if}}
    {{/get}}
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 9 · THE TOOLBOX ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Pitch on the left, the picks as compact rows on the right. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-split ns-split--wide-media">

      <div class="ns-split__body">
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "The toolbox"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-split__title">{{t "Books, tools and cheat sheets we actually use"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-split__lede">{{t "Hand-picked, not sponsored — every pick has earned its place in the library."}}</p>
        <div>
          <a href="/resources/" class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary ns-btn--lg">
            {{t "Browse the toolbox"}}{{> icons name="arrow-right" class="ns-btn__icon ns-btn__icon--nudge"}}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ns-split__media">
        {{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-resource" limit="4"}}
          {{#if posts}}
            <div class="ns-grid ns-grid--2 ns-grid--tight">
              {{#foreach posts}}
                <a href="{{url}}" class="ns-card ns-card--sm ns-card--interactive ns-card--row flex-row items-center gap-3">
                  <span class="ns-chip ns-chip--sm">
                    {{#has tag="#resource-type-book"}}{{> icons name="book-bookmark"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-tool"}}{{> icons name="wrench"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-video"}}{{> icons name="video"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-cheatsheet"}}{{> icons name="file-text"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-website"}}{{> icons name="globe"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-podcast"}}{{> icons name="microphone"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-repo"}}{{> icons name="git-fork"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-community"}}{{> icons name="users"}}{{else}}{{> icons name="cube"}}{{/has}}
                  </span>
                  <span class="min-w-0">
                    <span class="ns-truncate block text-sm font-bold leading-snug">{{title}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-card__meta">
                      {{#has tag="#resource-type-book"}}{{t "Book"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-tool"}}{{t "Tool"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-video"}}{{t "Video"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-cheatsheet"}}{{t "Cheat sheet"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-website"}}{{t "Website"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-podcast"}}{{t "Podcast"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-repo"}}{{t "Repo"}}{{else has tag="#resource-type-community"}}{{t "Community"}}{{else}}{{t "Resource"}}{{/has}}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </a>
              {{/foreach}}
            </div>
          {{else}}
            <div class="ns-empty">{{t "Resources coming soon."}}</div>
          {{/if}}
        {{/get}}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 10 · MEMBERSHIP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Tiers straight from Ghost Admin — see partials/members/tiers.hbs. Renders
     nothing at all if members are off or no tier exists, which is why there is
     no {{#if}} around it here. --}}
{{> "members/tiers"
    title=(t "Learn free. Fund it if it's worth it.")
    body=(t "Every lesson is readable without paying. A membership is how the hosting, the editing and the time get paid for — and it is cancellable in one click.")}}

{{!-- ── 11 · FAQ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Native <details>, so it works before Alpine loads and is findable by the
     browser's own in-page search. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-faq">
      <div>
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{> icons name="question"}}{{t "Questions"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-section-head__title">{{t "The ones we get asked most"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-section-head__sub">
          {{t "Anything else?"}}
          <a href="/docs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-300">{{t "The help centre has the long answers."}}</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-3">
        {{> "courses/faq-item"
            q=(t "Is it really free?")
            a=(t "Yes. Every course, every training lesson and every doc is readable without an account or a card. Membership pays for the site; it does not gate the curriculum.")}}
        {{> "courses/faq-item"
            q=(t "Do I need a Salesforce org?")
            a=(t "You need a free Developer Edition org, which Salesforce gives out at no cost and never expires. The first lesson walks you through creating one.")}}
        {{> "courses/faq-item"
            q=(t "What's the difference between the courses and the training?")
            a=(t "A course covers one subject in depth and can be taken on its own. The training is a single ordered path through all of them, from your first login to certification-ready.")}}
        {{> "courses/faq-item"
            q=(t "Why is there a separate app?")
            a=(t "This site is the public library — readable by anyone, indexed by search engines. app.namastesalesforce.com is the workspace: the lesson player, your progress and your certificates. Same account, same design system, different job.")}}
        {{> "courses/faq-item"
            q=(t "Will this get me certified?")
            a=(t "It covers the exam objectives and every lesson maps to one, but no course can sit the exam for you. Treat the training as the syllabus and the practice questions as the rehearsal.")}}
        {{> "courses/faq-item"
            q=(t "Can I contribute?")
            a=(t "Please do. The theme, the courses and the docs are open source — corrections, new lessons and new translations are all welcome, and authors are credited on everything they write.")}}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 12 · THE CLOSING BAND — open source + the newsletter ───────────────
     ONE ending, carrying both remaining asks. The open-source pitch is the
     reason to care and the newsletter is the thing to do about it, so they
     belong in the same breath; splitting them across two bands made the page
     end twice and asked for an email address a third time.

     The `--grid` variant supplies the pattern; no inline background. The two
     links that used to justify the deleted "everything in one place" band —
     the docs and the become-an-author page — live here, where a reader who
     has got this far is actually looking for them. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--dark ns-band--grid">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-news-band ns-news-band--dark">

      <div>
        <span class="ns-kicker ns-kicker--light">{{> icons name="git-branch"}}{{t "Open source"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-news-band__title">{{t "Built in the open, on Ghost"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-news-band__body">
          {{t "The whole platform — this theme, the courses, the docs — is an open-source project. Read the code, fix a typo or write a lesson: every contribution ships, and every author is credited."}}
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="https://github.com/imswarnil/Namaste-Salesforce" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ns-btn ns-btn--white">{{> icons name="github" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{t "Star on GitHub"}}</a>
          <a href="/docs/" class="ns-btn ns-btn--glass">{{> icons name="book-open"}}{{t "Docs & help center"}}</a>
          <a href="/become-author/" class="ns-btn ns-btn--glass">{{> icons name="user-plus" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{t "Write for us"}}</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      {{!-- The last ask. It earns its place by being specific about what gets
           sent — the only thing that actually changes a subscribe rate. --}}
      <div>
        <span class="ns-kicker ns-kicker--light">{{> icons name="mail"}}{{t "Newsletter"}}</span>
        <h2 class="ns-news-band__title">{{t "One email when something new lands"}}</h2>
        <p class="ns-news-band__body">
          {{t "Not a digest and not a drip campaign — a note when a course, a training section or a substantial rewrite is published, and nothing in between."}}
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5">
          {{> "members/subscribe" layout="stacked" tone="dark" cta=(t "Subscribe free")
              note=(t "No sponsors in your inbox, ever. One click to unsubscribe.")}}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── 13 · SPONSOR — the 728×90 leaderboard, last before the footer ────── --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sm">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    {{> "ads/leaderboard"}}
  </div>
</section>
